{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wellmade-surprised-chihuahua","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## The gap\n\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py::test_terraform_call_gets_tools_and_finalizer`\nhard-requires the OPTIONAL `grounding-terraform` extra (`python-hcl2==8.1.3`) but carries **no\n`importorskip` guard**. Every CI lane that deliberately installs without that extra therefore\nfails this test.\n\nThis is breaking `main` NOW. Run 33905162633 (test.yml on branch main, sha ee2c54f881d6):\n\n```\nFAILED tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py::test_terraform_call_gets_tools_and_finalizer\nAssertionError: assert 'abstain' == 'refuted'\n1 failed, 15435 passed, 92 skipped in 415.78s\n```\n\nat `test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:118`:\n```\nresult = lookup(\"aws_instance.web\", module_path=\"infra\")\nassert result[\"evidence\"][\"outcome\"] == \"refuted\"   # got 'abstain'\n```\n\n## Root cause — VERIFIED by controlled experiment\n\nThe install step SUCCEEDS; this is not a resolution failure. `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py::open_session`\ndoes `if not available(): pending = \"missing_extra\"`, and every query then returns a closed\nABSTENTION rather than a verdict. `available()` is `_capabilities.is_available(\"grounding_terraform\")`,\nwhose probe is `hcl2`. So without the extra the tool abstains, and the test asserting `refuted` fails.\n\nExperiment in a throwaway worktree at ee2c54f881d6:\n- hcl2 absent -> `1 failed, 15 passed`, identical assertion. Reproduced.\n- `uv pip install python-hcl2==8.1.3`, NO other change -> `16 passed`. Confirmed.\n\n## Why it appeared now, and why only on some lanes\n\n`6dde7dffe6b2` (\"Add optional Terraform structural grounding\") added this test module. Its two\nsibling modules from the SAME commit — `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py` and\n`test_terraform_index.py` — each carry a module-scope `pytest.importorskip(\"hcl2\")`. This module\ngot none. That inconsistency sat latent.\n\n`c57057f41` (\"Enable the grounding-terraform extra\") then added `--extra grounding-terraform` to\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` (the gating Verified lane) and `_optionality.yml` — but\nNOT to `test.yml`. So the gating lane installs the extra and passes, while every `test.yml` sweep\nlane installs without it (`uv pip install --resolution lowest-direct '.[dev,agents]'` at line 413;\n`.[dev,reviewbot,ui]` at 320/352/380) and fails.\n\nConfirmed in the same run: `build-and-test / pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)` PASSED with\n`uv sync --locked ... --extra grounding-terraform` and `+ python-hcl2==8.1.3` in its log, while\n`sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` and `sweep (py3.14)` both failed with the byte-identical\nassertion.\n\n## Regression, not pre-existing — VERIFIED\n\n`sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` had NEVER failed before this run. Earlier red main-health\nruns failed on DIFFERENT jobs:\n```\n33875177644 (09-04 12:54, 1af450654) success — sweep (windows) only\n33846424069 (06:55) failure — sweep (windows), sweep (macos, full suite)\n33840948374 (05:33) failure — sweep (windows), scanner-integration\n33824556786 (01:07) failure — sweep (windows), pytest (ubuntu, py3.13)\n33792688019 (09-03 18:48) success — sweep (windows) only\n```\nIntroduced between `1af450654` (green) and `ee2c54f881d6`.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a **FUNCTION-SCOPE** `pytest.importorskip(\"hcl2\")` immediately before the real-parse query in\n`test_terraform_call_gets_tools_and_finalizer`, just before the `lookup = next(...)` call around\nline 117.\n\n**Function scope, not module scope.** This is the only test in the file that needs a real HCL\nparse; the other 15 exercise routing, the extra-less contract, and read-set freshness. A\nmodule-scope guard would over-skip and discard exactly the coverage the lean lanes SHOULD keep —\nincluding the tests that verify correct behaviour when the extra is absent, which are the most\nvaluable ones to run on an extra-less lane.\n\n**Guard the test; do NOT widen the sweep lanes' installs.** The lower-bound lane's own header\nstates its contract: \"The floorless optional web extras (ui/reviewbot/pricing) are out of scope —\ntheir tests self-skip via importorskip\". The repo already has the sanctioned TWO-SIDED mechanism\n(`tests/_extra_guard.py`, bug 599e-77da-29dd-482d): tests guard with `importorskip`, and the\ngating lane sets `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1` — which DOES install grounding-terraform — so the guard\nbecomes a hard error there if the extra ever silently disappears. That gives skip-on-lean and\nfail-loudly-on-gating from one mechanism. Adding the extra to every sweep lane would instead make\nthe lean lanes not lean, defeating their purpose.\n\n**No dependency floor should be raised.** `python-hcl2==8.1.3` is an EXACT pin, so there is no\nfloor to fail. Any floor change here would be aimed at the wrong cause.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — `test_terraform_call_gets_tools_and_finalizer` calls `pytest.importorskip(\"hcl2\")`\n      before its real-parse query, and the module's other 15 tests still RUN (not skip) without\n      the extra installed.\n- [ ] AC2 — In an install WITHOUT `grounding-terraform`, `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py`\n      reports `15 passed, 1 skipped`. Demonstrate with actual output.\n- [ ] AC3 — In an install WITH the extra, all 16 tests run and pass. Demonstrate with actual output.\n- [ ] AC4 — Under the gating lane's configuration (`REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1`), the guard is a HARD\n      ERROR rather than a silent skip, so a silently-vanished extra cannot hide as a skip on the\n      lane that is supposed to prove it. Verify against `tests/_extra_guard.py`'s existing\n      mechanism rather than inventing a second one.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNot changing `terraform_tools.py`'s abstention behaviour — abstaining without the extra is CORRECT\nand is what the other 15 tests pin. Not adding `grounding-terraform` to any `test.yml` sweep lane.\nNot raising any dependency floor. Not touching `sweep (windows)`, which is a separate long-standing\nfailure with its own ticket (`unsuited-locustal-incatern`) blocked on an operator scope decision.\n\n## File impact\n\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py`","id":"87b8-1339-383f-43f6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_terraform_call_gets_tools_and_finalizer lacks an importorskip guard, so it fails on every CI lane without the optional grounding-terraform extra: main is red across the sweep lanes"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788546848446183001,"uuid":"83ae1073-7e17-456c-bf35-74c47b7e0258"}